---
import DocShell from '../../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../../lib/nav';

const toc = [
   { id: 'record', label: 'Start a recording' },
   { id: 'permission', label: 'Screen Recording permission on macOS' },
   { id: 'problems', label: 'Troubleshooting' },
   { id: 'privacy', label: 'Before you share a recording' },
];
---

<DocShell
   title="Record a screen reader session"
   summary="<p>Record the screen while VoiceOver or NVDA reads a page. Attach the video and the log of announcements to a bug report, to show what happened on screen and what the screen reader said.</p>"
   links={docsLinks}
   toc={toc}
>
   <section>
      <h2 id="record">Start a recording</h2>
      <p>
         Pass <code>--recording</code> with a file path when you start the session. Stopping
         the session finishes the file.
      </p>
      <pre><code>a1 sr start --sr voiceover --recording ./recordings/checkout.mov http://localhost:3000/checkout
a1 sr next
a1 sr checkpoint "sent the form"
a1 sr stop</code></pre>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt>VoiceOver, macOS</dt>
         <dd>Records to a <code>.mov</code> file. Video only: a1 does not ask for the microphone, so the file has no sound.</dd>
         <dt>NVDA, Windows</dt>
         <dd>Records to an <code>.mp4</code> file.</dd>
         <dt>Simulated</dt>
         <dd>Cannot record. It has no window. Save its transcript in its place.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>
         Stopping also writes the transcript next to the video. For
         <code>checkout.mov</code> the file is <code>checkout.transcript.md</code>. Each
         announcement has a timestamp, so a reviewer can match what was said to a moment in
         the video.
      </p>
      <p>
         Keep each recording to one behavior. Add <code>sr checkpoint</code> at the moments a
         reviewer should look for.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="permission">Screen Recording permission on macOS</h2>
      <p>
         macOS gives the permission to the app that runs the command, not to a1. Run
         <code>a1</code> from Terminal and Terminal needs it. Run it from your editor or an
         agent and that app needs it.
      </p>
      <p>
         Grant it in System Settings, under Privacy &amp; Security, then Screen &amp; System
         Audio Recording. Restart the app afterwards. Then check from that same app:
      </p>
      <pre><code>a1 doctor --task reader --sr voiceover --recording</code></pre>
      <p>
         This records a short test video, deletes it, and reports whether recording works.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="problems">Troubleshooting</h2>
      <dl class="defs defs--wide">
         <dt>It works in Terminal and fails in your editor</dt>
         <dd>The editor does not have the permission. Grant it and restart the editor.</dd>
         <dt>The command fails before recording starts</dt>
         <dd>Install Chrome, Edge, Brave, or Chromium. VoiceOver and NVDA sessions open the page in a browser that is installed on the system.</dd>
         <dt><code>doctor</code> reports <code>requires-setup</code></dt>
         <dd>Run <code>a1 setup</code>.</dd>
         <dt>The file is empty</dt>
         <dd>Run <code>a1 sr stop</code>. The file is finished when the session stops.</dd>
      </dl>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="privacy">Before you share a recording</h2>
      <p>
         A recording shows the whole screen: the page, the browser, menus, notifications, and
         anything else in view. Use test data, and watch the file before you attach it.
      </p>
      <p>
         A recording shows one run of one build. Note the URL, the browser, and the screen
         reader with it, so a reviewer knows what they are looking at.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
